WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:04.090
- This butterfly was once
thought to be extinct.

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:06.740
Though rediscovered, it
remains one of the world's

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.230
rarest and most elusive butterflies.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:13.213
This is the Palos Verdes Blue Butterfly.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.250
This butterfly is as
elusive as it is beautiful.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.210
And the brilliance of its blue wings

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.313
are only visible when it opens them.

00:00:28.270 --> 00:00:29.530
The wings are distinctive

00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:31.693
with their brilliant silvery blue color.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:36.190
The butterfly was thought
to be extinct in the 1980s,

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:39.370
when it seemed to
disappear without a trace.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.730
It wasn't until the 1990s that

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.513
this visually striking
butterfly was spotted again.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:50.210
Biologists were surprised and
delighted in its existence.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:53.343
And a breeding program was
begun to build up the species.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:57.230
Though captive breeding
has helped bolster numbers,

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.100
the population is still low enough

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.410
to remain on the endangered list.

00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.610
Through careful nurturing and management,

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:07.453
this small but mighty butterfly
has a fighting chance.

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:11.313
This is the Palos Verdes Blue Butterfly.

